				<div id="bodyContent" class="vector-body" aria-labelledby="firstHeading" data-mw-ve-target-container>
					<div class="vector-body-before-content">
							<div class="mw-indicators">
		</div>

						<div id="siteSub" class="noprint">From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia</div>
					</div>
					<div id="contentSub"><div id="mw-content-subtitle"></div></div>
					
					
					<div id="mw-content-text" class="mw-body-content"><div class="mw-subjectpageheader">
</div><div class="mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output" lang="en" dir="ltr" data-mw-parsoid-version="0.24.0.0-alpha18" data-mw-html-version="2.8.0"><section data-mw-section-id="0" id="mwAQ"><div class="shortdescription nomobile noexcerpt noprint searchaux" style="display:none" about="#mwt1" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Short description","href":"./Template:Short_description"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Moduli scheme of subschemes of a scheme, represents the flat-family-of-subschemes functor"}},"i":0}}]}'>Moduli scheme of subschemes of a scheme, represents the flat-family-of-subschemes functor</div><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_short_description"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Short_description_is_different_from_Wikidata"/></span>
<p id="mwAw">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algebraic_geometry" title="Algebraic geometry" id="mwBA">algebraic geometry</a>, a branch of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematics" title="Mathematics" id="mwBQ">mathematics</a>, a <b id="mwBg">Hilbert scheme</b> is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scheme_theory" title="Scheme theory" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBw">scheme</a> that is the parameter space for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Closed_subscheme" title="Closed subscheme" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCA">closed subschemes</a> of some projective space (or a more general projective scheme), refining the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chow_variety" title="Chow variety" id="mwCQ">Chow variety</a>.  The Hilbert scheme is a disjoint union of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Projective_subscheme" title="Projective subscheme" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCg">projective subschemes</a> corresponding to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hilbert_polynomial" title="Hilbert polynomial" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCw">Hilbert polynomials</a>. The basic theory of Hilbert schemes was developed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Grothendieck" title="Alexander Grothendieck" about="#mwt2" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"harvs","href":"./Template:Harvs"},"params":{"first":{"wt":"Alexander"},"1":{"wt":"txt"},"last":{"wt":"Grothendieck"},"authorlink":{"wt":"Alexander Grothendieck"},"year":{"wt":"1961"}},"i":0}}]}'>Alexander<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Grothendieck</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt2"> </span><span about="#mwt2">(</span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#CITEREFGrothendieck1961" about="#mwt2" class="mw-selflink-fragment">1961</a><span about="#mwt2">)</span>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hironaka's_example" title="Hironaka's example" id="mwDQ">Hironaka's example</a> shows that non-projective varieties need not have Hilbert schemes.</p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" id="mwDg" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}'/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwDw" aria-labelledby="Hilbert_scheme_of_projective_space"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Hilbert_scheme_of_projective_space">Hilbert scheme of projective space</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Hilbert_scheme&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: Hilbert scheme of projective space"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwEA">The Hilbert scheme <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt5" id="mwEQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbf{Hilb}(n)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbf {Hilb} (n)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="bold">H</mi>
          <mi mathvariant="bold">i</mi>
          <mi mathvariant="bold">l</mi>
          <mi mathvariant="bold">b</mi>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>n</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbf {Hilb} (n)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/11e2d17ddbe1172aaf44c5d7d30b7bf073d17661" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:8.265ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbf {Hilb} (n)}"/></span> of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt6" id="mwEg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{P}^n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{n}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{n}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/7e712abd7ff167cfb12ffa7c8c9bf7b0029cf192" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:2.639ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{n}}"/></span> classifies closed subschemes of projective space in the following sense: For any <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Locally_Noetherian_scheme" title="Locally Noetherian scheme" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEw">locally Noetherian scheme</a> <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt3" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwFA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"S"}},"i":0}}]}'>S</span>, the set of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt4" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwFQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"S"}},"i":0}}]}'>S</span>-valued points</p>

<dl id="mwFg"><dd id="mwFw"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt7" id="mwGA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\operatorname{Hom}(S, \\mathbf{Hilb}(n))"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \operatorname {Hom} (S,\mathbf {Hilb} (n))}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>Hom</mi>
        <mo>⁡<!-- ⁡ --></mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>S</mi>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="bold">H</mi>
          <mi mathvariant="bold">i</mi>
          <mi mathvariant="bold">l</mi>
          <mi mathvariant="bold">b</mi>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>n</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \operatorname {Hom} (S,\mathbf {Hilb} (n))}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/d7dddb0466b38b2f7006d7ee804870248d84e1c4" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:17.449ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \operatorname {Hom} (S,\mathbf {Hilb} (n))}"/></span></dd></dl>

<p id="mwGQ">of the Hilbert scheme is naturally isomorphic to the set of closed subschemes of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt12" id="mwGg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{P}^n \\times S"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{n}\times S}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo>×<!-- × --></mo>
        <mi>S</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{n}\times S}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/a46c97112299f02d0277d4792a94bb197ead04aa" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:6.978ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{n}\times S}"/></span> that are <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flat_morphism" title="Flat morphism" id="mwGw">flat</a> over <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt8" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwHA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"S"}},"i":0}}]}'>S</span>. The closed subschemes of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt13" id="mwHQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{P}^n \\times S"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{n}\times S}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo>×<!-- × --></mo>
        <mi>S</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{n}\times S}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/a46c97112299f02d0277d4792a94bb197ead04aa" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:6.978ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{n}\times S}"/></span> that are flat over <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt9" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwHg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"S"}},"i":0}}]}'>S</span> can informally be thought of as the families of subschemes of projective space parameterized by <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt10" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwHw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"S"}},"i":0}}]}'>S</span>. The Hilbert scheme  <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt14" id="mwIA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbf{Hilb}(n)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbf {Hilb} (n)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="bold">H</mi>
          <mi mathvariant="bold">i</mi>
          <mi mathvariant="bold">l</mi>
          <mi mathvariant="bold">b</mi>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>n</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbf {Hilb} (n)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/11e2d17ddbe1172aaf44c5d7d30b7bf073d17661" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:8.265ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbf {Hilb} (n)}"/></span> breaks up as a disjoint union of pieces <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt15" id="mwIQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbf{Hilb}(n, P)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbf {Hilb} (n,P)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="bold">H</mi>
          <mi mathvariant="bold">i</mi>
          <mi mathvariant="bold">l</mi>
          <mi mathvariant="bold">b</mi>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>n</mi>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mi>P</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbf {Hilb} (n,P)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/3e5a983f96e02fb15e733a46e57b786b5972dd60" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:11.044ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbf {Hilb} (n,P)}"/></span> corresponding to the Hilbert scheme of the subschemes of projective space with Hilbert polynomial <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt11" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwIg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"P"}},"i":0}}]}'>P</span>. Each of these pieces is projective over <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt16" id="mwIw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\operatorname{Spec}(\\Z)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \operatorname {Spec} (\mathbb {Z} )}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>Spec</mi>
        <mo>⁡<!-- ⁡ --></mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Z</mi>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \operatorname {Spec} (\mathbb {Z} )}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/b2f78f6479a69210705f06b1a0c7eeb1077c3b4f" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:8.009ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \operatorname {Spec} (\mathbb {Z} )}"/></span>.</p>

<section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwJA" aria-labelledby="Construction_as_a_determinantal_variety"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Construction_as_a_determinantal_variety">Construction as a determinantal variety</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Hilbert_scheme&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Construction as a determinantal variety"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwJQ">Grothendieck constructed the Hilbert scheme <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt17" id="mwJg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbf{Hilb}(n)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbf {Hilb} (n)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="bold">H</mi>
          <mi mathvariant="bold">i</mi>
          <mi mathvariant="bold">l</mi>
          <mi mathvariant="bold">b</mi>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>n</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbf {Hilb} (n)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/11e2d17ddbe1172aaf44c5d7d30b7bf073d17661" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:8.265ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbf {Hilb} (n)}"/></span> of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt18" id="mwJw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle n}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>n</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle n}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/a601995d55609f2d9f5e233e36fbe9ea26011b3b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.395ex; height:1.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle n}"/></span>-dimensional projective <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt19" id="mwKA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{P}^n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{n}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{n}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/7e712abd7ff167cfb12ffa7c8c9bf7b0029cf192" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:2.639ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{n}}"/></span> space as a subscheme of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grassmannian" title="Grassmannian" id="mwKQ">Grassmannian</a> defined by the vanishing of various <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Determinant" title="Determinant" id="mwKg">determinants</a>. Its fundamental property is that for a scheme <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt20" id="mwKw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"T"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle T}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>T</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle T}</annotation>
