          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>m</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mi>Q</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>m</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle {\textbf {Gr}}(Q(m)-P_{X}(m),Q(m))}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/09e111d1c6727d12a31a2a843e775a90d4613984" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:27.237ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle {\textbf {Gr}}(Q(m)-P_{X}(m),Q(m))}"/></span>. This will give an embedding of the piece of the Hilbert scheme corresponding to the Hilbert polynomial <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt46" id="mwTg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"P_X"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle P_{X}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>P</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>X</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle P_{X}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/8348dd8ce7e6f7f4778ee01fa5bdc7b828afd98c" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:3.125ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle P_{X}}"/></span> into this Grassmannian.</p>

<p id="mwTw">It remains to describe the scheme structure on this image, in other words to describe enough elements for the ideal corresponding to it. Enough such elements are given by the conditions that the map <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt47" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwUA" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;math&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Math&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;''I&lt;sub>X&lt;/sub>''(''m'') ⊗ ''S''(''k'') → ''S''(''k'' + ''m'')&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><i>I<sub>X</sub></i>(<i>m</i>) ⊗ <i>S</i>(<i>k</i>) → <i>S</i>(<i>k</i> + <i>m</i>)</span> has rank at most <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt48" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwUQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"dim(&apos;&apos;I&lt;sub>X&lt;/sub>&apos;&apos;(&apos;&apos;k&apos;&apos; + &apos;&apos;m&apos;&apos;))"}},"i":0}}]}'>dim(<i>I<sub>X</sub></i>(<i>k</i> + <i>m</i>))</span> for all positive <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt49" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwUg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"k"}},"i":0}}]}'>k</span>, which is equivalent to the vanishing of various determinants. (A more careful analysis shows that it is enough just to take <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt50" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwUw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;k&apos;&apos; {{=}} 1"}},"i":0}}]}'><i>k</i> = 1</span>.)</p>

<section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwVA" aria-labelledby="Universality"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Universality">Universality</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Hilbert_scheme&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: Universality"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwVQ">Given a closed subscheme <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt52" id="mwVg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"Y \\subset \\mathbb{P}^n_k=X"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle Y\subset \mathbb {P} _{k}^{n}=X}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>Y</mi>
        <mo>⊂<!-- ⊂ --></mo>
        <msubsup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>k</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle Y\subset \mathbb {P} _{k}^{n}=X}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/1fb9427279bfde81381553bba02c0a1221c472eb" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:12.589ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle Y\subset \mathbb {P} _{k}^{n}=X}"/></span> over a field with Hilbert polynomial <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt53" id="mwVw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"P"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle P}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>P</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle P}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/b4dc73bf40314945ff376bd363916a738548d40a" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.745ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle P}"/></span>, the Hilbert scheme <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt51" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwWA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"H=&apos;&apos;&apos;Hilb&apos;&apos;&apos;(&apos;&apos;n&apos;&apos;, &apos;&apos;P&apos;&apos;)"}},"i":0}}]}'>H=<b>Hilb</b>(<i>n</i>, <i>P</i>)</span> has a universal subscheme <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt54" id="mwWQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"W \\subset X \\times H"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle W\subset X\times H}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>W</mi>
        <mo>⊂<!-- ⊂ --></mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo>×<!-- × --></mo>
        <mi>H</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle W\subset X\times H}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/1760dca78bdafbd6da19c3c783dc155518dcce63" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:12.418ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle W\subset X\times H}"/></span> flat over <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt55" id="mwWg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H}">
  <semantics>
