    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle Z}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/1cc6b75e09a8aa3f04d8584b11db534f88fb56bd" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.68ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle Z}"/></span>. This construction is functorial by taking pullbacks of families. Given <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt96" id="mwmw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"f: T&apos; \\to T"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle f:T'\to T}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>f</mi>
        <mo>:</mo>
        <msup>
          <mi>T</mi>
          <mo>′</mo>
        </msup>
        <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
        <mi>T</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle f:T'\to T}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/6bfe86bf7ec01b2388e929feccc6cf4de8ad05b8" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:10.871ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle f:T'\to T}"/></span>, there is a family <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt97" id="mwnA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"f^*Z = Z\\times_TT&apos;"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle f^{*}Z=Z\times _{T}T'}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>f</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>∗<!-- ∗ --></mo>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mi>Z</mi>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <mi>Z</mi>
        <msub>
          <mo>×<!-- × --></mo>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>T</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <msup>
          <mi>T</mi>
          <mo>′</mo>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle f^{*}Z=Z\times _{T}T'}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/bbd0bc4087ec2c093f4e0c9eb7ae9914d029adac" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:15.468ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle f^{*}Z=Z\times _{T}T'}"/></span> over <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt98" id="mwnQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"T&apos;"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle T'}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>T</mi>
          <mo>′</mo>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle T'}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/4b32d735f4fbb6eff3b35ed3dc1005a069d0b2e5" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:2.405ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle T'}"/></span>.</p>

<section data-mw-section-id="8" id="mwng" aria-labelledby="Representability_for_projective_maps"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Representability_for_projective_maps">Representability for projective maps</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Hilbert_scheme&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8" title="Edit section: Representability for projective maps"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwnw">If the structure map <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt99" id="mwoA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"X \\to S"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle X\to S}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
        <mi>S</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle X\to S}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/3496d15a6102a8883ca2f5d33afd25d2d7dc9f4d" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:7.093ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle X\to S}"/></span> is projective, then this functor is represented by the Hilbert scheme constructed above. Generalizing this to the case of maps of finite type requires the technology of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algebraic_space" title="Algebraic space" id="mwoQ">algebraic spaces</a> developed by Artin.<sup about="#mwt102" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-1" id="mwog"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwow"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwpA">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwpQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="9" id="mwpg" aria-labelledby="Relative_Hilbert_scheme_for_maps_of_algebraic_spaces"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Relative_Hilbert_scheme_for_maps_of_algebraic_spaces">Relative Hilbert scheme for maps of algebraic spaces</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Hilbert_scheme&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9" title="Edit section: Relative Hilbert scheme for maps of algebraic spaces"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwpw">In its greatest generality, the Hilbert functor is defined for a finite type map of algebraic spaces <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt103" id="mwqA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"f\\colon X \\to B"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle f\colon X\to B}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>f</mi>
        <mo>:<!-- : --></mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
        <mi>B</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle f\colon X\to B}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/d1f4dd766fa96e2a0b48f4e71119a75383f0489d" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:9.671ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle f\colon X\to B}"/></span> defined over a scheme <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt104" id="mwqQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"S"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle S}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>S</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle S}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/4611d85173cd3b508e67077d4a1252c9c05abca2" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.499ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle S}"/></span>. Then, the Hilbert functor is defined as<sup about="#mwt107" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-2" id="mwqg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwqw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwrA">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwrQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<dl id="mwrg"><dd id="mwrw"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt108" id="mwsA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\underline{\\text{Hilb}}_{X/B}:(Sch/B)^{op} \\to Sets"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle {\underline {\text{Hilb}}}_{X/B}:(Sch/B)^{op}\to Sets}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <munder>
              <mtext>Hilb</mtext>
              <mo>_<!-- _ --></mo>
            </munder>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>X</mi>
            <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
              <mo>/</mo>
            </mrow>
            <mi>B</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo>:</mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>S</mi>
        <mi>c</mi>
        <mi>h</mi>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mo>/</mo>
        </mrow>
        <mi>B</mi>
        <msup>
          <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>o</mi>
            <mi>p</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
        <mi>S</mi>
        <mi>e</mi>
        <mi>t</mi>
        <mi>s</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle {\underline {\text{Hilb}}}_{X/B}:(Sch/B)^{op}\to Sets}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/b51cf9ed31c276aacc59e9da8e6f9a08b242ff0f" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.031ex; margin-bottom: -0.307ex; width:28.535ex; height:3.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle {\underline {\text{Hilb}}}_{X/B}:(Sch/B)^{op}\to Sets}"/></span></dd></dl>
<p id="mwsQ">sending <i id="mwsg">T</i> to </p>
<dl id="mwsw"><dd id="mwtA"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt109" id="mwtQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\underline{\\text{Hilb}}_{X/B}(T) = \\left\\{ Z \\subset X\\times_BT : \n\\begin{align}\n&amp;Z \\to T \\text{ is flat, proper,} \\\\\n&amp;\\text{and of finite presentation}\n\\end{align}\n\\right\\}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle {\underline {\text{Hilb}}}_{X/B}(T)=\left\{Z\subset X\times _{B}T:{\begin{aligned}&amp;Z\to T{\text{ is flat, proper,}}\\&amp;{\text{and of finite presentation}}\end{aligned}}\right\}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <munder>
              <mtext>Hilb</mtext>
              <mo>_<!-- _ --></mo>
            </munder>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>X</mi>
            <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
              <mo>/</mo>
            </mrow>
            <mi>B</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>T</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <mrow>
          <mo>{</mo>
          <mrow>
            <mi>Z</mi>
            <mo>⊂<!-- ⊂ --></mo>
            <mi>X</mi>
            <msub>
              <mo>×<!-- × --></mo>
              <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
                <mi>B</mi>
              </mrow>
            </msub>
            <mi>T</mi>
            <mo>:</mo>
            <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
              <mtable columnalign="right left right left right left right left right left right left" rowspacing="3pt" columnspacing="0em 2em 0em 2em 0em 2em 0em 2em 0em 2em 0em" displaystyle="true">
                <mtr>
                  <mtd></mtd>
                  <mtd>
                    <mi>Z</mi>
                    <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
                    <mi>T</mi>
                    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
                      <mtext> is flat, proper,</mtext>
                    </mrow>
                  </mtd>
                </mtr>
                <mtr>
                  <mtd></mtd>
                  <mtd>
                    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
                      <mtext>and of finite presentation</mtext>
                    </mrow>
                  </mtd>
                </mtr>
              </mtable>
            </mrow>
          </mrow>
          <mo>}</mo>
        </mrow>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle {\underline {\text{Hilb}}}_{X/B}(T)=\left\{Z\subset X\times _{B}T:{\begin{aligned}&amp;Z\to T{\text{ is flat, proper,}}\\&amp;{\text{and of finite presentation}}\end{aligned}}\right\}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/84b5b714c12cbc1019795650d92316644f2ea29e" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -2.505ex; width:58.617ex; height:6.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle {\underline {\text{Hilb}}}_{X/B}(T)=\left\{Z\subset X\times _{B}T:{\begin{aligned}&amp;Z\to T{\text{ is flat, proper,}}\\&amp;{\text{and of finite presentation}}\end{aligned}}\right\}}"/></span>.</dd></dl>
<p id="mwtg">This functor is not representable by a scheme, but by an algebraic space. Also, if <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt110" id="mwtw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"S = \\text{Spec}(\\Z)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle S={\text{Spec}}(\mathbb {Z} )}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>S</mi>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mtext>Spec</mtext>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Z</mi>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle S={\text{Spec}}(\mathbb {Z} )}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/dbc25f38f2aeda14449e809d5415078a52f5303a" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:12.607ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle S={\text{Spec}}(\mathbb {Z} )}"/></span>, and <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt111" id="mwuA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"X\\to B"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle X\to B}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
        <mi>B</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle X\to B}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/47e293dd629fadde2afa076c6d3266ca8088b74f" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:7.358ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle X\to B}"/></span> is a finite type map of schemes, their Hilbert functor is represented by an algebraic space.</p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="10" id="mwuQ" aria-labelledby="Examples_of_Hilbert_schemes"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Examples_of_Hilbert_schemes">Examples of Hilbert schemes</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Hilbert_scheme&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10" title="Edit section: Examples of Hilbert schemes"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mwug" aria-labelledby="Fano_schemes_of_hypersurfaces"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Fano_schemes_of_hypersurfaces">Fano schemes of hypersurfaces</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Hilbert_scheme&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11" title="Edit section: Fano schemes of hypersurfaces"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwuw">One of the motivating examples for the investigation of the Hilbert scheme in general was the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fano_scheme" title="Fano scheme" class="mw-redirect" id="mwvA">Fano scheme</a> of a projective scheme. Given a subscheme <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt112" id="mwvQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"X \\subset \\mathbb{P}^n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle X\subset \mathbb {P} ^{n}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo>⊂<!-- ⊂ --></mo>
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle X\subset \mathbb {P} ^{n}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/59ec74d93cc805a1c25dcee28747a3c4aa8fec7f" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:7.717ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle X\subset \mathbb {P} ^{n}}"/></span> of degree <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt113" id="mwvg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"d"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle d}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>d</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle d}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/e85ff03cbe0c7341af6b982e47e9f90d235c66ab" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.216ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle d}"/></span>, there is a scheme <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt114" id="mwvw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"F_k(X)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle F_{k}(X)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>F</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>k</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle F_{k}(X)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/3815452a5bcfe305e1ed7bab46e252d0980c1ca8" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:6.373ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle F_{k}(X)}"/></span> in <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt115" id="mwwA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{G}(k, n)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {G} (k,n)}">
  <semantics>
