          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{n}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/7e712abd7ff167cfb12ffa7c8c9bf7b0029cf192" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:2.639ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{n}}"/></span>, meaning it is a degree one embedding of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt120" id="mwxQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{P}^k"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{k}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>k</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{k}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/7cc094c5a1ac8968285785524e9b989ddda21b5d" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:2.509ex; height:2.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{k}}"/></span>.<sup about="#mwt123" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_3-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:0-3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:0-3" id="mwxg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwxw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyA">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyQ">]</span></span></a></sup> For smooth surfaces in <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt124" id="mwyg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{P}^3"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{3}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>3</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{3}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/7fb80175bc622b3936c7a0438fc690b2ec410b4f" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:2.475ex; height:2.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{3}}"/></span> of degree <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt125" id="mwyw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"d \\geq 3"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle d\geq 3}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>d</mi>
        <mo>≥<!-- ≥ --></mo>
        <mn>3</mn>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle d\geq 3}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/7ebd85f457285fae5a6938211a05b373a4263d6d" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.505ex; width:5.477ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle d\geq 3}"/></span>, the non-empty Fano schemes <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt126" id="mwzA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"F_k(X)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle F_{k}(X)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>F</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>k</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle F_{k}(X)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/3815452a5bcfe305e1ed7bab46e252d0980c1ca8" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:6.373ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle F_{k}(X)}"/></span> are smooth and zero-dimensional. This is because lines on smooth surfaces have negative self-intersection.<sup about="#mwt127" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_3-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:0-3" id="mwzQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwzg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwzw">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0A">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mw0Q" aria-labelledby="Hilbert_scheme_of_points"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Hilbert_scheme_of_points">Hilbert scheme of points</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Hilbert_scheme&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12" title="Edit section: Hilbert scheme of points"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mw0g">Another common set of examples are the Hilbert schemes of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt128" id="mw0w" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle n}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>n</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle n}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/a601995d55609f2d9f5e233e36fbe9ea26011b3b" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.395ex; height:1.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle n}"/></span>-points of a scheme <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt129" id="mw1A" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"X"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle X}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>X</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle X}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/68baa052181f707c662844a465bfeeb135e82bab" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.98ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle X}"/></span>, typically denoted <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt130" id="mw1Q" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"X^{[n]}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle X^{[n]}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>X</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo stretchy="false">[</mo>
            <mi>n</mi>
            <mo stretchy="false">]</mo>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle X^{[n]}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/90afdd96f8d116eae452fbff609ce7bd935121b5" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:4.13ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle X^{[n]}}"/></span>. For a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riemann_surface" title="Riemann surface" id="mw1g">Riemann surface</a> X, <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt131" id="mw1w" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"X^{[n]}=S^nX=X^n/S_n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle X^{[n]}=S^{n}X=X^{n}/S_{n}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>X</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo stretchy="false">[</mo>
            <mi>n</mi>
            <mo stretchy="false">]</mo>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <msup>
          <mi>S</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <msup>
          <mi>X</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mo>/</mo>
        </mrow>
        <msub>
          <mi>S</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle X^{[n]}=S^{n}X=X^{n}/S_{n}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/ae83c77ac6f272e9f6804c1fbcb5a55b1bf2f292" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:22.068ex; height:3.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle X^{[n]}=S^{n}X=X^{n}/S_{n}}"/></span>.  For <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt132" id="mw2A" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{P}^2"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{2}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>2</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{2}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/02e892a2d48ff09d2f95b0e8b8eb419d42e179c6" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:2.475ex; height:2.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{2}}"/></span> there is a nice geometric interpretation where the boundary loci <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt133" id="mw2Q" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"B \\subset H"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle B\subset H}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>B</mi>
        <mo>⊂<!-- ⊂ --></mo>
        <mi>H</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle B\subset H}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/d73f0d480f6969eeb6816dbedaeab311b5d2b9dc" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:6.926ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle B\subset H}"/></span> describing the intersection of points can be thought of parametrizing points along with their tangent vectors. For example, <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt134" id="mw2g" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"(\\mathbb{P}^2)^{[2]}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle (\mathbb {P} ^{2})^{[2]}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>2</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <msup>
          <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo stretchy="false">[</mo>
            <mn>2</mn>
            <mo stretchy="false">]</mo>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle (\mathbb {P} ^{2})^{[2]}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/4755891c94a4dad0dccd43258ce7dd8af6d9b0b4" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:6.253ex; height:3.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle (\mathbb {P} ^{2})^{[2]}}"/></span> is the blowup <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt135" id="mw2w" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"Bl_{\\Delta}(\\mathbb{P}^2\\times\\mathbb{P}^2/S_2)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle Bl_{\Delta }(\mathbb {P} ^{2}\times \mathbb {P} ^{2}/S_{2})}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>B</mi>
        <msub>
          <mi>l</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="normal">Δ<!-- Δ --></mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>2</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo>×<!-- × --></mo>
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>2</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mo>/</mo>
        </mrow>
        <msub>
          <mi>S</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>2</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle Bl_{\Delta }(\mathbb {P} ^{2}\times \mathbb {P} ^{2}/S_{2})}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/c3450cbb4fdd54bdd134c1ea0034dab0fe7249df" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:17.299ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle Bl_{\Delta }(\mathbb {P} ^{2}\times \mathbb {P} ^{2}/S_{2})}"/></span> of the diagonal<sup about="#mwt138" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-4"}}'><a href="#cite_note-4" id="mw3A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw3Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3g">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3w">]</span></span></a></sup> modulo the symmetric action.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="13" id="mw4A" aria-labelledby="Degree_d_hypersurfaces"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Degree_d_hypersurfaces">Degree d hypersurfaces</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Hilbert_scheme&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13" title="Edit section: Degree d hypersurfaces"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mw4Q">The Hilbert scheme of degree k hypersurfaces in <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt139" id="mw4g" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{P}^n"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{n}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{n}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/7e712abd7ff167cfb12ffa7c8c9bf7b0029cf192" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:2.639ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{n}}"/></span> is given by the projectivization <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt140" id="mw4w" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{P}(\\Gamma(\\mathcal{O}(k)))"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} (\Gamma ({\mathcal {O}}(k)))}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi mathvariant="normal">Γ<!-- Γ --></mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi class="MJX-tex-caligraphic" mathvariant="script">O</mi>
          </mrow>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>k</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} (\Gamma ({\mathcal {O}}(k)))}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/6a5d029aff5a2c25b8fc7b71f51de666a2a9d7d1" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:11.362ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} (\Gamma ({\mathcal {O}}(k)))}"/></span>. For example, the Hilbert scheme of degree 2 hypersurfaces in <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt141" id="mw5A" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{P}^1"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{1}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{1}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/5e38808c13ecc929e128079b70c1642554e2a4b3" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:2.475ex; height:2.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{1}}"/></span> is <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt142" id="mw5Q" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\mathbb{P}^2"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{2}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">P</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>2</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{2}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/02e892a2d48ff09d2f95b0e8b8eb419d42e179c6" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:2.475ex; height:2.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {P} ^{2}}"/></span> with the universal hypersurface given by</p>
<dl id="mw5g"><dd id="mw5w"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt143" id="mw6A" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\text{Proj}(k[x_0,x_1][\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma]/(\\alpha x_0^2 + \\beta x_0x_1 + \\gamma x_1^2)) \\subseteq \\mathbb{P}_{x_0,x_1}^1\\times\\mathbb{P}^2_{\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle {\text{Proj}}(k[x_{0},x_{1}][\alpha ,\beta ,\gamma ]/(\alpha x_{0}^{2}+\beta x_{0}x_{1}+\gamma x_{1}^{2}))\subseteq \mathbb {P} _{x_{0},x_{1}}^{1}\times \mathbb {P} _{\alpha ,\beta ,\gamma }^{2}}">
  <semantics>
